#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:7
#: 1a05fb9f0c7a4392885a4031b96de246
msgid "Serial Passthrough"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:9
#: 26ee860c0af441978764e3d5ee95b3e6
msgid "\"Serial Passthrough\" allows the autopilot to route serial protocol messages between serial ports on the autopilot including the USB port.  This can be used to configure a sensors or devices (which have a serial interface) without disconnecting it from the autopilot using a USB connection. It is also possible to pass data from any serial port to another serial port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:12
#: 4ad186a7601e48b099f28c0440072179
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:14
#: 479b87db43704f31b33d822b5286812d
msgid "The sensor or device (with a serial interface) should already be connected to one of the autopilot's serial ports.  Ideally it should already be working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:15
#: 4eddcb0f3f0444f8a6cb7e63b29e1f4a
msgid "Connect the autopilot to a PC using a USB cable and connect with a Ground Station (i.e. Mission Planner, QGC, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:17
#: e44683183ef14e33a588f90376ceb808
msgid "On most F7 and H7 boards, a second USB virtual serial port also appears when you connect via USB to the autopilot and is assigned the last SERIALx port in ArduPilot for SLCAN use. This can also be used for serial device configuration by changing :ref:`SERIAL_PASS1<SERIAL_PASS1>` to that port's number. This allows the autopilot to remain connected to a Ground Control Station, and still use passthrough to a sensor for configuration simultaneously on the PC via its configuration program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:19
#: f731dc129ab44573812ea4ae4cc3f802
msgid "Its best if the sensor already can be detected and used by ArduPilot first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:20
#: 0867c671e7d349088a3c48e339a459c8
msgid "Be sure to set each port's baud rate appropriately using the ``SERIALx_BAUD`` parameters (USB ports automatically use the passthrough port's baud rate and do not need to be changed). The rates may be different for each port. ArduPilot will do the buffering.  For example, if attempting passthrough to the first GPS, :ref:`SERIAL3_BAUD <SERIAL3_BAUD>` should normally be set to 230400 but you may check the GPS driver's \"autobauding\" by looking at the ground stations Message window soon after startup. Additionally, many sensor drivers ignore what is set for this parameter, since its hardcoded in the driver, but it MUST be set when using the passthrough feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:26
#: ac23d5425c2b4d63a1e743c6cd04e68c
msgid "The default for :ref:`SERIAL_PASS1<SERIAL_PASS1>` (the first serial port to be interconnected) defaults to SERIAL0, the primary USB port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:27
#: baa2c61e4261441889ff4b2098fc97f1
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL_PASSTIMO <SERIAL_PASSTIMO>` timeout to a length of time (in seconds) that gives you enough time to connect with the sensor's configuration software. 30 to 60 seconds is a good choice but setting it to zero will remain in passthrough until reboot occurs. Setting this to -1 will allow the connection to remain even after rebooting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:28
#: 7c33bf32af134cb68626f4cbcfc688fe
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL_PASS2 <SERIAL_PASS2>` to the number of the serial port connected to the sensor.  I.e. \"2\" if the sensor is connected to Telem2/Serial2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:29
#: 98069e27cc5548d2bab5e0ce4d522e91
msgid "Press the \"Disconnect\" button on the ground station but leave the USB cable from the PC to the autopilot connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:31
#: 0910f9d5c0674af2be4cf312d45ba3ff
msgid "some GCS do not have any easy means to \"Disconnect\" or will immediately try to reconnect. In those cases just close the GCS application entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:33
#: 890cd8eb7b2d4d0696c86c06e34e8969
msgid "Open the sensor's configuration software and connect to the autopilot's COM port.  If all goes well the configuration software should work as it does when the PC is directly connected to the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:35
#: af268bfc48024b038234356d9b87b23f
msgid "If the configuration fails to connect there are some things to try:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:37
#: 91887528ac6a4f9f9f02862fa779a5c0
msgid "Some configuration software will not allow connecting to the autopilot's COM port by default but may have a option to display all available COM ports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-passthrough.rst:38
#: b4421062915d4ecb82df5d20f2edc5a9
msgid "If no serial messages are received from the PC the timeout will expire and :ref:`SERIAL_PASS2 <SERIAL_PASS2>` will revert to -1"
msgstr ""

